      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll start by reading both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me analyze what's happening:\n\n- Value `141` triggers the `PopulationCodec` path in `getCodec`\n- A `BufferedInputStream` wrapping a 9-zero-byte `ByteArrayInputStream` is passed\n- The `BufferedInputStream`'s read-ahead behavior causes it to drain the entire `ByteArrayInputStream` into its internal buffer\n- The assertion verifies the `ByteArrayInputStream` is fully drained (0 available)\n\nLet me write the improved test with better clarity:Now let me compile-check the test:The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names with descriptive ones (`defaultCodec`, `codecSpecifierBytes`, `underlyingStream`, `bufferedStream`) and adds comments explaining why value `141` triggers the PopulationCodec path, what the zero bytes mean, and why the `BufferedInputStream`'s read-ahead drains the underlying `ByteArrayInputStream`."
